Message-ID: <BEA6A318CB196546AA5184CE0F37447001BEA83A@UTHEVS3.mail.uthouston.edu>

We use a stationarity test based on the Kolmogorov-Smirnov 
test of difference between distributions on subsets of the test segment. As Eric 
Zivot pointed out, this is once again a test of one kind of stationarity, but it 
is more robust than testing for varying means or variances. In any case, all 
stationarity tests that I am aware of pertain to weak stationarity, and this is 
usually sufficient. Unfortunately, I do not have a S-Plus implementation that I 
could forward to you.

 

